{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-133764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/assets/f6cbd594db6ab2454844d744ce1b776c3f561c4a6295abb9222ad2416c9f9292.png)\n\nDetermine the equation of the trend line shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha256" "66358a926a18bdb8f3ba9abb44684a0fbb20660e1fb0fca83a4061794283eebd"} {"question" "q-133764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(2,8)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(8,5).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-8}{8-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{6} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-\\frac{1}{2}$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can find this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(2,8):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x+b \\\\ 8 & =-\\frac{1}{2}(2)+b \\\\ 8 & =-1+b \\\\ 9 & =b \\\\ b & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x+9.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha256" "66358a926a18bdb8f3ba9abb44684a0fbb20660e1fb0fca83a4061794283eebd"} {"question" "q-133764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4eaca168cbeeff1c1cf3d52dff58f794508f36c55057855efe9bb215c66bdea4"} {"question" "q-133764" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha256" "66358a926a18bdb8f3ba9abb44684a0fbb20660e1fb0fca83a4061794283eebd"} {"question" "q-133764" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+7"] ["math" "y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+9"] ["math" "y=-\\frac{3}{5}x+9"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{2}x+7"] ["math" "y=\\frac{3}{5}x+6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha256" "66358a926a18bdb8f3ba9abb44684a0fbb20660e1fb0fca83a4061794283eebd"} {"question" "q-133764" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+9"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha256" "66358a926a18bdb8f3ba9abb44684a0fbb20660e1fb0fca83a4061794283eebd"} {"question" "q-134002" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/assets/80cb125155a1a55404f2257196560a4e563e75c12d4c87c24b0464e509d7a0fa.png)\n\nWhich of the following is the trend line of the scatter plot above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha256" "66358a926a18bdb8f3ba9abb44684a0fbb20660e1fb0fca83a4061794283eebd"} {"question" "q-134002" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The plot shows that the data points are scattered along a straight line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/assets/18cba39701d1ec8ead1281a68fad5dab2b1f584aa396eddcfa306c4961c6397e.png)\n\nWe see that the line $s$ best fits the given data set." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha256" "66358a926a18bdb8f3ba9abb44684a0fbb20660e1fb0fca83a4061794283eebd"} {"question" "q-134002" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4eaca168cbeeff1c1cf3d52dff58f794508f36c55057855efe9bb215c66bdea4"} {"question" "q-134002" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha256" "66358a926a18bdb8f3ba9abb44684a0fbb20660e1fb0fca83a4061794283eebd"} {"question" "q-134002" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "p"] ["math" "q"] ["math" "r"] ["math" "s"] ["text" "There is no linear trend in the data"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha256" "66358a926a18bdb8f3ba9abb44684a0fbb20660e1fb0fca83a4061794283eebd"} {"question" "q-134002" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "s"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha256" "66358a926a18bdb8f3ba9abb44684a0fbb20660e1fb0fca83a4061794283eebd"} {"question" "q-134018" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/assets/da0836fa401981d7a0a254a136036a0ead7e3be8eefff5ef3fdfb31070759f0a.png)\n\nDetermine the equation of the trend line shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha256" "66358a926a18bdb8f3ba9abb44684a0fbb20660e1fb0fca83a4061794283eebd"} {"question" "q-134018" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(1,3)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(5,8).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-3}{5-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=\\frac{5}{4}$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{5}{4}x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can find this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(1,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{5}{4}x+b \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{5}{4}(1)+b \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{5}{4}+b \\\\ 12 & =5+4b \\\\ 7 & =4b \\\\ b & =\\frac{7}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=\\frac{5}{4}x+\\frac{7}{4}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha256" "66358a926a18bdb8f3ba9abb44684a0fbb20660e1fb0fca83a4061794283eebd"} {"question" "q-134018" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4eaca168cbeeff1c1cf3d52dff58f794508f36c55057855efe9bb215c66bdea4"} {"question" "q-134018" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha256" "66358a926a18bdb8f3ba9abb44684a0fbb20660e1fb0fca83a4061794283eebd"} {"question" "q-134018" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{3}{2}x+1"] ["math" "y=\\frac{3}{2}x+\\frac{7}{4}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{5}{4}x+1"] ["math" "y=\\frac{5}{4}x+\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{5}{4}x+\\frac{7}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha256" "66358a926a18bdb8f3ba9abb44684a0fbb20660e1fb0fca83a4061794283eebd"} {"question" "q-134018" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{5}{4}x+\\frac{7}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha256" "66358a926a18bdb8f3ba9abb44684a0fbb20660e1fb0fca83a4061794283eebd"} {"question" "q-134025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/assets/c8f6d0161777412704a9a80c0336af04a6968454d421913055024b6d0cf11c71.png)\n\nEstimate the slope of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round your answer to the nearest $0.5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha256" "66358a926a18bdb8f3ba9abb44684a0fbb20660e1fb0fca83a4061794283eebd"} {"question" "q-134025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/assets/b50fd1636cc2e1bb9d150eaba9cc25a3ccedff77e607bf22853004332a7c4ddc.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(3,6)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(5,3).$\n\nTherefore, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-6}{5-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{2} \\\\  & =-1.5\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha256" "66358a926a18bdb8f3ba9abb44684a0fbb20660e1fb0fca83a4061794283eebd"} {"question" "q-134025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4eaca168cbeeff1c1cf3d52dff58f794508f36c55057855efe9bb215c66bdea4"} {"question" "q-134025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha256" "66358a926a18bdb8f3ba9abb44684a0fbb20660e1fb0fca83a4061794283eebd"} {"question" "q-134025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-0.5"] ["math" "-1.5"] ["math" "-2.5"] ["math" "0.5"] ["math" "1.5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha256" "66358a926a18bdb8f3ba9abb44684a0fbb20660e1fb0fca83a4061794283eebd"} {"question" "q-134025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1.5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha256" "66358a926a18bdb8f3ba9abb44684a0fbb20660e1fb0fca83a4061794283eebd"} {"question" "q-134026" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/assets/75f8a5bd247b1f792fd60640fbbd2f864359abe48110d59f1fbe0da00eae4ed5.png)\n\nEstimate the slope of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round your answer to the nearest $0.5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha256" "66358a926a18bdb8f3ba9abb44684a0fbb20660e1fb0fca83a4061794283eebd"} {"question" "q-134026" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/assets/384610cdc149e8b4eaa6df1d3eea1715dda88543c57679553875d226814f6cf7.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(-1,4)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(1,2).$\n\nTherefore, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-4}{1-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{2} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha256" "66358a926a18bdb8f3ba9abb44684a0fbb20660e1fb0fca83a4061794283eebd"} {"question" "q-134026" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4eaca168cbeeff1c1cf3d52dff58f794508f36c55057855efe9bb215c66bdea4"} {"question" "q-134026" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha256" "66358a926a18bdb8f3ba9abb44684a0fbb20660e1fb0fca83a4061794283eebd"} {"question" "q-134026" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-2.5"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "1.5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010570/state.json" "file_sha25